      "message": "Hi, added some the expectation images for this new test. Something to point out:\n\nI tried using pdfium_diff on the x86 and the arm mac image, it gave a diff of 0.00% but failed. Checking on the CI bots, we had a difference of 2/3 pixels. However, that difference of 2/3 pixels seems to be sufficient enough for it to still fail (since we expect 0 pixels different), which is why 2 images were needed.\n\nFew ideas are:\n- Landing https://pdfium-review.googlesource.com/c/pdfium/+/141270: Quick to do and useful if it happens anywhere else\n\n- We could leave it as is if it is a special case, but wouldn\u0027t make much sense to duplicate it and has less \"constexpr-ness\"\n\n- Updating CompareBitmapToPngWithFuzzyExpectationSuffix() to also allow a maximum difference of a certain amount of pixels, either as a bool flag or by default.\n\nWould prefer option 1 personally, and am adding this to the thread there as well, but let me know which approach we should consider.",
